Hmm, wait: if the SW isn't registered yet (Turbo.offline.start is async), `getRegistration()` may resolve undefined initially and `connect()` would show "off". Then when the SW registers, the state won't refresh. Minor. But for correctness, I could listen to the `navigator.serviceWorker` controllerchange or just re-check in `toggle`. Also if the user clicks "Turn on" before the SW is ready, `navigator.serviceWorker.ready` in `#subscribe` waits for registration. Good. Then `#refresh` after subscribe will see the subscription.

Hmm, `#refresh` uses `#subscription()` which uses `getRegistration()` — after subscribe it will exist. OK.

Also for a robustness: after subscribing, if `Notification.permission === "granted"` and subscription exists → turnOn. Fine.

